# Alembic Migration Update Policy

When updating database schema with Alembic in this project:

- Use Alembic CLI commands only for migration workflow.
- Do not manually create migration files in `alembic/versions/`.
- Do not manually edit migration revision identifiers or generated migration structure unless explicitly requested for a special case.

## Required workflow

```bash
# Generate migration from model/schema changes
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe_change"

# Apply latest migration
alembic upgrade head
```

## Never do this by default

- Manually add a new migration file under `alembic/versions/`.
- Handcraft a migration file instead of generating it via Alembic CLI.

## Keep `migration/` scripts in sync

When an Alembic revision is created or updated, update the related script(s) under `migration/` in the same change so deployment/runtime migration scripts stay aligned with `alembic/versions/`.
